and copy only the error messages (do not let it continue if it starts evicting pods unexpectedly).

Also run:

oc get pdb -A

and

oc get pods -A | grep -E 'Terminating|Pending'

Why I want these

On a Single Node OpenShift cluster, the SR-IOV operator drains the node before applying NIC changes. The drain usually fails because of one of these reasons:

A PodDisruptionBudget (PDB) prevents eviction.

A pod cannot be evicted.

A static/control-plane pod is blocking the drain.

Another workload is preventing the node from being drained.


Once we see the drain error or the PDBs, we'll know exactly which resource is preventing the SR-IOV operator from completing the Reboot_Required state.
